 the most conservative and strategic opening move available. By flipping only one piece and staying within the central 4x4 box (rows C-F, cols 3-6), it limits the opponent\'s counter-play options. It avoids placing pieces on the outer edges (like E2 or H4) and prevents giving the opponent easy access to C-squares or corners this early in the game.\n\nAnswer: (C, 5)'}
